{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to Moses in Midian.</b> After He said to him in the wilderness, He returned and said to him in Midian." "<b>For all the men have died</b> etc. — who are they? Datan and Aviram were alive, etc. That is to say: they were blind — one cannot say so, for it is written in the parashah of Korah: ״the eyes of those men shall be put out.״ They had no sons — one cannot say so, for it is written ״their wives and their sons and their little ones.״ They were lepers — one cannot say so, for they were within the camp of Israel, as it is written: ״Get you up from about the tabernacle of Korah, Datan, and Aviram.״ Perforce, they were poor. And according to the plain sense: all the men — the relatives of the Egyptian whom you killed."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The comment engages with the midrashic reading (cited via the opening formula attributed to Rashi's discussion) that 'all the men who sought your life' refers specifically to Datan and Aviram, who survived by being impoverished. The phrase 'who are they?' introduces the problem that Datan and Aviram were still alive despite the verse saying 'all the men have died.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:09.136873347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}